      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a theoretical possibility that low-frequency signals could be used for covert transmission, especially if the devices are communicating through non-standard channels. However, consumer smart devices rarely possess the sophisticated hardware needed to reliably transmit complex audio data through subtle light or power pulses undetected. Your next crucial step should be physically isolating the devices—unplugging them entirely—to confirm the behavior stops completely. If the issue persists when unplugged, the problem lies with an external factor, not the devices themselves.",
